---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageIntro from "../components/PageIntro.astro";

const updated = "July 28, 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Harvous"
  description="How Harvous collects, uses, and protects your data."
>
  <section class="border-b border-[var(--color-rule)]">
    <PageIntro>
      <div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-[var(--color-ink-faint)]">Legal</div>
      <h1 class="mt-3 font-display text-5xl leading-[1.0] md:text-6xl">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-[var(--color-ink-faint)]">Last updated {updated}</p>
    </PageIntro>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-16 md:py-20" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 80ms;">
    <div class="prose-letter space-y-8">
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)]">Overview</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]">
          Harvous is a Bible study notes app operated by Testament Made LLC ("we," "us"). This policy
          explains what information we collect, how we use it, and the choices you have. By using
          Harvous, you agree to this policy.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)]">Information we collect</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]">
          <strong class="text-[var(--color-ink)]">Account information.</strong> When you sign up, we use
          Clerk for authentication. Clerk may collect your email address, name, and sign-in details
          needed to verify your identity.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]">
          <strong class="text-[var(--color-ink)]">Your content.</strong> We store the notes, threads,
          spaces, highlights, and related study data you create in Harvous. This content is tied to
          your account and is private by default.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]">
          <strong class="text-[var(--color-ink)]">Usage and device data.</strong> We collect technical
          and product-usage information to keep Harvous reliable and to understand how the app is used
          — for example browser or device type, app version, pages or screens viewed, feature usage,
          and error reports. This may be associated with your account (such as your user id, and
          limited profile details like email or name) so we can improve the product.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]">
          <strong class="text-[var(--color-ink)]">Email and messaging.</strong> If you have an account
          or subscribe to updates, we may store your email and related preferences so we can send
          product or service communications (for example, onboarding or important account notices).
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)]">How we use your information</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]">
          We use your information to provide and improve Harvous: syncing your notes across devices,
          authenticating your account, analyzing product usage, responding to support requests,
          sending relevant product or service emails, and protecting the service from abuse. We do
          not sell your personal information.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)]">Sharing</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]">
          Your notes are private unless you choose to share them. When you create a share link, only
          the content you explicitly share becomes accessible to people with that link. We use trusted
          service providers who process data on our behalf under appropriate agreements, including
          Clerk (authentication), Supabase (data storage), PostHog (product analytics), and Audienceful
          (email). These providers only receive what they need to perform their services for us.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]">
          We configure analytics with privacy in mind: we do not enable session recording by default,
          we do not turn on broad automatic click capture, and we respect browser Do Not Track
          settings when they are enabled.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)]">Cookies</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]">
          Harvous uses cookies and similar technologies (including local storage) to keep you signed
          in, remember basic preferences, and support product analytics. You can control cookies
          through your browser settings, though some features may not work without them. Enabling Do
          Not Track in your browser may limit analytics collection.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)]">Data retention and deletion</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]">
          We retain your account and content for as long as your account is active. You may request
          deletion of your account and associated data by contacting us. Some information may be kept
          briefly where required for legal or security purposes, or for a limited time in analytics or
          email systems after deletion while those systems process the request.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)]">Contact</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]">
          Questions about this policy or your data? Email
          <a
            class="underline decoration-[var(--color-rule)] underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-[var(--color-ink)]"
            href="mailto:derek@harvous.com"
          >
            derek@harvous.com
          </a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
